# 000400-000499/20070523T132417Z_132924275.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=119d|+Algorithm %3D%3D%0A%0AThe operation of diff is based on solving the [[Longest_common_subsequence_problem%7CLongest Common Subsequence]] (LCS) problem. In the LCS problem, you have two sequences of items:%0A%0A        a b c d f g h j q z%0A%0A        a b c d e f g i j k r x y z%0A%0Aand you want to find the longest sequence of items that is present in both original sequences in the same order.%0AThat is, you want to find a new sequence which can be obtained from the first sequence by deleting some items, and from the secend sequence by deleting other items.%0AYou also want this sequence to be as long as possible.%0AIn this case it is%0A%0A        a b c d f g j z%0AFrom the longest common subsequence it's only a small step to get diff%2Dlike output:%0A%0A        e   h i   k   q r x y %0A        %2B   %2D %2B   %2B   %2D %2B %2B %2B%0A%0A%3D%3D |=3af9|
